        "id": 1066075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-28T08:17:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How big do you expect the request to be? \n\nI half-expected some sort of streaming here so that the complete aquery/cquery output doesn\u0027t need to be in RAM at the same time, but I don\u0027t know how big they are.\n\nWhat are the limits of encoding/gob ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 110,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 110,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "22031f853ab8c2d4636adec4fd50101f16126182",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b149a66_ff039380",
        "filename": "bazel/bazel_proxy.go",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1605027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-28T20:34:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The response might become quite large as our tree grows (especially wrt aquery). Our previous implementation (issuing subcommands) also did not deal with streaming, so I\u0027m tempted to defer this issue until a future CL.\n\nFrom what I understand of the libraries I\u0027m calling, we do stream the output, but we indeed don\u0027t stream the decoding.\n\nProcessing the results in a streaming fashion is a tricky problem even beyond this protocol, esp wrt. aquery, because Bazel\u0027s aquery output is `proto`. This proto is Bazel\u0027s ActionGraphContainer, and we parse the entire output as such. We\u0027d need to be a bit more clever to parse individual fields of the ActionGraphContainer.",
      "parentUuid": "3f3c02e1_065cfa5c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 110,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 110,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "22031f853ab8c2d4636adec4fd50101f16126182",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
